# The AI gateway's secret settings, read by the gateway container (services/gateway/
# README.md, Provider keys). The gateway holds the only provider keys on the platform:
# no other service is given one, and none is ever pasted into code, a chat or a log.

# Which services may call the gateway: a JSON object of service name to the base64url
# public key of that service's Ed25519 key pair, on one line inside single quotes, such as
# '{"django-systems":"<public key>","flask-systems":"<public key>","node-systems":"<public
# key>","web":"<public key>"}'. `just gateway-token keygen <service> <private key file>`
# makes a key pair and prints the entry to put here; the private half goes to the service
# itself (docs/DEPLOY.md, Provider keys and service keys). One entry for each service that
# calls a model: a service without an entry is refused.
LB_SERVICE_KEYS=

# Groq: a key from the Groq console.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Cloudflare Workers AI: the account ID, and an API token with the Workers AI permission.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# OpenRouter: a key made for this gateway alone, with a small credit limit.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# There is deliberately no NVIDIA key here. The NVIDIA API catalog's trial terms forbid
# production use, so it stays a local, private-experiments provider that production
# leaves off every chain.
